# The market is wider than the FPGA prices.
#
# Pricing finds fair value within the spread by comparing against every tick
# in it at once, so the hardware covers at most 16 ticks; wider markets
# aren't quoted. As with an invalid book, the app skips requoting but leaves
# its resting quotes alone. When the spread is back to 16 ticks or less, it
# requotes.
#
# No timer: a jumping mid would widen the credit and blur the test.
#
# Participants: 2 and 3 provide the book.

latency market_data 5_000
latency order_entry 10_000
end 20_000_000

# 100.00 x 100.01: quote 99.99 x 100.02.
0            2 enter 1 B 500 100.00
0            3 enter 1 S 500 100.01

# The offer moves to 100.17: 17 ticks wide. No requote.
3_000_000    3 enter 2 S 1500 100.17
3_000_100    3 cancel 1

# The bid drops to 99.95: 22 ticks. Still no requote.
6_000_000    2 enter 2 B 100 99.95
6_000_100    2 cancel 1

# A bid at 100.01 brings the spread to exactly 16 ticks: quoted again. Fair
# value is 100.01 + 16 ticks x 100 / 1600 = 100.02, on a tick: 100.01 x 100.03.
9_000_000    2 enter 3 B 100 100.01

# A normal market returns: 100.01 x 100.02.
12_000_000   3 enter 3 S 500 100.02
